+# Entity Resolution
+
+This example extracts entities from a document, resolves references between
+them, and saves the result as an interactive graph.
+
+!!! tips "Motivation"
+
+    Entity resolution is useful when a document contains cross-references such
+    as dates, parties, payments, obligations, or dependencies. A structured
+    schema can capture both the extracted facts and the relationships needed to
+    resolve them.
+
+## Define the entity schema
+
+Each entity includes a stable id, source quotes, properties, and dependencies on
+other entities.
+
+```ts
+import Instructor from "@/instructor"
+import OpenAI from "openai"
+import { z } from "zod"
+
+const PropertySchema = z.object({
+  key: z.string(),
+  value: z.string(),
+  resolved_absolute_value: z.string()
+})
+
+const EntitySchema = z.object({
+  id: z.number(),
+  subquote_string: z.array(z.string()),
+  entity_title: z.string(),
+  properties: z.array(PropertySchema),
+  dependencies: z.array(z.number())
+})
+
+const DocumentExtractionSchema = z.object({
+  entities: z.array(EntitySchema)
+})
+```
+
+## Extract entities from text
+
+The system prompt asks the model to extract facts and resolve references.
+Instructor validates the result against the entity graph schema.
+
+```ts
+const oai = new OpenAI({
+  apiKey: process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY ?? undefined,
+  organization: process.env.OPENAI_ORG_ID ?? undefined
+})
+
+const client = Instructor({
+  client: oai,
+  mode: "TOOLS"
+})
+
+const askAi = async (input: string) => {
+  return client.chat.completions.create({
+    messages: [
+      {
+        role: "system",
+        content:
+          "You are an entity resolution system. Extract and resolve a list of entities from the following document."
+      },
+      {
+        role: "user",
+        content: input
+      }
+    ],
+    model: "gpt-4o",
+    response_model: {
+      schema: DocumentExtractionSchema,
+      name: "Document Extraction"
+    },
+    max_retries: 3,
+    seed: 1
+  })
+}
+```
+
+## Visualize the graph
+
+The example includes a helper that converts the extracted entities into an HTML
+graph using `vis-network`.
+
+```ts
+import { saveHtmlDocument } from "./exampleGraphMaker"
+
+const model = await askAi(content)
+saveHtmlDocument(model, "entityGraph")
+```
+
+The full runnable example lives in
+`examples/resolving-complex-entitities/index.ts`.
+
+!!! note "Adapting the example"
+
+    For production use, tighten the schema around your domain-specific entities
+    and keep `subquote_string` fields so reviewers can trace every structured
+    result back to the source text.
