+# Multiple Search Queries
+
+This example converts a natural-language request into several typed search
+queries that can be executed in parallel.
+
+!!! tips "Motivation"
+
+    Users often ask for several things in one sentence. A structured extraction
+    step can split the request into separate searches while preserving the
+    search title, query text, and destination type.
+
+## Define the search schema
+
+Each search has a title, a query, and a type. The example uses `VIDEO` and
+`EMAIL`, but you can replace these with the destinations your application uses.
+
+```ts
+import Instructor from "@/instructor"
+import OpenAI from "openai"
+import { z } from "zod"
+
+const SearchSchema = z.object({
+  title: z.string().describe("Title of the request"),
+  query: z.string().describe("Query to search for relevant content"),
+  type: z.enum(["VIDEO", "EMAIL"]).describe("Type of search")
+})
+
+const MultiSearchSchema = z.object({
+  searches: z.array(SearchSchema).describe("List of searches")
+})
+```
+
+## Segment the request
+
+Ask the model to segment the user request into the structured response model.
+
+```ts
+const oai = new OpenAI({
+  apiKey: process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY ?? undefined,
+  organization: process.env.OPENAI_ORG_ID ?? undefined
+})
+
+const client = Instructor({
+  client: oai,
+  mode: "FUNCTIONS"
+})
+
+async function segment(data: string) {
+  return client.chat.completions.create({
+    messages: [
+      {
+        role: "system",
+        content: "You are a helpful assistant."
+      },
+      {
+        role: "user",
+        content: `Consider the data below:\n${data} and segment it into multiple search queries`
+      }
+    ],
+    model: "gpt-4-1106-preview",
+    response_model: {
+      schema: MultiSearchSchema,
+      name: "Multi Search"
+    },
+    max_tokens: 1000,
+    temperature: 0.1
+  })
+}
+```
+
+## Execute searches
+
+The output can be mapped into your own search functions.
+
+```ts
+async function executeMultiSearch(multiSearch: z.infer<typeof MultiSearchSchema>) {
+  return Promise.all(
+    multiSearch.searches.map(search => {
+      console.log(`Searching for ${search.title} with ${search.query} using ${search.type}`)
+    })
+  )
+}
+```
+
+The full runnable example lives in
+`examples/multiple_search_queries/index.ts`.
+
+!!! note "Extending search types"
+
+    Add more enum values when your application supports additional backends such
+    as `DOCS`, `TICKETS`, `CRM`, or `TRANSCRIPTS`.
